Bayar's Comic, Issue 3         NannyMUD Times                         Page 7

The Long Road

Bayar: I think I got the hang of it now, thanks to the map. I think it is the
  only thing good about the booklet. But no time for chit-chat, I have to see
  that letter...

The post office <e>.

Bayar: Now, how in the world will I find my mailbox here? There must be 
  thousands of boxes here! Oh, wait, I see it now, in the section marked NEW.
  Lets see... a letter from our great God:

    "I have done some research and I came up with a possible solution: 
    you have to become a wizard and create yourself a portal to your own 
    world. It isn't as simple as it may seem.
    
    Becoming a wizard is no childs play. You will have to work hard, gain 
    wealth and fame, engage in epic battles and so on. My advice for you 
    is to start working on the quests in The Book of Quests. Some of them 
    are simple, while others are nearly impossibe to complete.
    
    Good luck on your mission!"
    
Bayar: Seems I have my work cut out for me. Ok, a Book of Quests... should 
  be a bookshop around here somewhere.

The tourist information office <w>.

Clerk: Welcome young adventurer! Have you come for a wizard booklet?

Bayar: Actually, no. I was looking for a bookshop.

Clerk: Trust me. Tell me a wizards name from the list.

Bayar: Fine. Show me... Brom!

The clerk hands over Bayar a booklet about Brom.

You recieve a questpoint along with the booklet.

Bayar: Well, that was fairly easy, thanks for that tip. Now about the 
  bookshop...

Clerk: You can find one on Malkuth Street North of here.

Bayar: Thank you for all you have done for me. Oh... and here is your booklet 
  back.

A bookshop <n>.

Bayar: I would like a book of quests, please.

Quintus: That will be 50 coins.

Bayar: Do you cccept IOU's?

Quintus: No, only money.

Bayar: How about this newbie booklet? I will sell it for almost nothing, 
  just get me rid of it.
  
Quintus: Get me 50 coins and it is yours.

An open yard <e w n s nw>.

Beggar: Give 2 coins to a poor beggar.

Bayar: Sorry, I don't have any money on me, I'm looking for money too.

Beggar: Then get lost! This is my spot!

The beggar missed Bayar.

Bayar: This guy is not playing around!

The beggar hit Bayar hard on the head.

Bayar falls to the ground.

Bayar: Idiot! Don't play with me!

Bayar picks op a knife convinientely placed near him.

The beggar missed Bayar.

Bayar stabbed the beggar in the leg.

The beggar annoyed Bayar.

Bayar grazed the beggar's back.

Bayar: Time to finish this! DIIEEEE!!!!

Bayar ripped the beggars abdomen to bits.

Beggar dies.

Bayar: Lets see... he had about 100 coins on him. More than enough to buy that
  book.

A bookshop <n>.

Bayar: 50 coins. Now, about my book...

Quintus hands over a book of quests to Bayar along with a questpoint.

Bayar:This is getting better and better!


